UPDATE inventory SET quantity = 15 WHERE id = 1;

DELETE FROM inventory WHERE id = 2;

DESCRIBE HISTORY inventory;

questions.question:
A data engineer runs the following two statements against a Delta Lake table named events (event_id INT, event_type STRING, event_ts TIMESTAMP):

Statement 1: INSERT INTO events SELECT * FROM staged_events;
Statement 2: INSERT OVERWRITE events SELECT * FROM staged_events;

Both statements are valid and no errors occur. Which statement correctly describes the write semantics of each statement?
